ui: stop a lingering OSC 11 reader thread from eating keystrokes

query_background() spawned a thread doing stdin.read() that, on a terminal
that never replied to OSC 11, outlived the 150ms probe and competed with
crossterm's EventStream reader for every keystroke thereafter. Each read
raced; under a synthetic pty (tu) roughly every second or third key was
swallowed, making lofi appear to eat input.

Replace the thread+channel reader with an inline nix::poll loop on stdin's
fd bounded by the same deadline. No thread is spawned, so nothing is left
reading stdin after we return — the bug class is gone, not just narrowed.
